# Rule name: Tenant organisation (X-ORGANIZATION-ID)


## Rule

Tenant isolation is enforced **server-side**, from the JWT. Front-end filters and
client-supplied `organisation_id` values are never an authorization mechanism.

### Vocabulary

| Term | Source | Role |
|------|--------|------|
| **JWT organisation** (home) | `organisation_id` claim of the user JWT | The user's real organisation — **absolute bound** |
| **Current organisation** (acting) | `X-ORGANIZATION-ID` header; absent = JWT organisation | Organisation the user is working in |
| **Tree(org)** | `organisation_closures` (self + descendants) | Perimeter an organisation manages |

- The header is accepted only if current org ∈ tree(JWT org); otherwise **403**.
- Invalid header (empty, non-integer, < 1) → **400**.

### Visibility (user JWT)

```text
read  = flags(current org) ∩ tree(JWT org)
write = tree(current org) ∩ tree(JWT org)
```

- No flag → **current organisation only**.
- `mine`, `children`, `deep` widen reads downward.
- `shared`, `catalog` go **upward** (ancestors / catalogue): never on private data
  (→ **400**); allowed only on shareable resources, **read-only**, for rows explicitly
  marked as shared (e.g. `catalog = true`).
- A row that exists but is out of scope, accessed by id → **404** (no existence leak).
- A payload attaching a resource to a foreign organisation → **403**.

### Tokens

- **User JWT**: always bounded as above.
- **Module (M2M) token**: unrestricted by design. Never use a module token to serve an
  end-user request. If a module backend must, it filters by organisation itself and
  documents it in `docs/module.yaml` (`access`).

### Callers (Play, module frontends, module backends)

- Call `platform-api` (and any tenant-aware service) on behalf of a user with the **user
  JWT** + `X-ORGANIZATION-ID` when the user switched organisation.
- Do not pass `organisation_id` as a query/body parameter to "filter" — the server decides.
- Ask for wider scopes explicitly with flags (`children=true`, `deep=true`) only where the
  product needs it (e.g. Deepidoo admin views).
- Expect fewer results / 404 when moving from unfiltered to filtered endpoints; do not
  work around it with a module token.

### Services owning tenant data

- Apply the same semantics: header → current org, bounded by the JWT org tree, in the
  repository/service layer — not only in route handlers or UI.
- Include the tenant perimeter in every cache key of tenant-filtered responses.
- Tests: allowed case + forbidden cases (foreign header 403, foreign id 404, foreign
  payload 403, upward flag on private data 400) + module token behaviour.

### Reference implementation

`platform-api` — `app/core/deps.py` (`get_acting_organisation_id`),
`app/core/tenant_scope.py`, `app/core/tenant_deps.py`, `app/repositories/tenant_clause.py`;
repo rule `.cursor/rules/11-tenant-organisation.mdc`.
